module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.InvertibleCompare
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SheafHom
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartier

/-!
# A local criterion for a closed subscheme to be an effective Cartier divisor

A closed subscheme of a scheme `X` is an effective Cartier divisor when its ideal sheaf is an
invertible `𝒪_X`-module, and invertibility is the global statement that tensoring by the ideal
sheaf is an equivalence. This file reduces it to local data: it suffices to produce, on each
member of an open cover of `X`, a rank-one dual basis for the ideal sheaf — a section `e`
generating it and a dual coordinate `λ` with `λ(e) = 1`.

This is the shape in which the forward direction of Stacks Tag 01WS is wanted: on an affine
open where the ideal is generated by a single nonzerodivisor `t`, the generator is `t` and the
dual coordinate is "divide by `t`". Producing that dual basis is no longer missing: it is
`Stacks.Divisors.dualBasisOneOfPrincipal` in `Divisors/IdealSheafSections.lean`, which with the
reduction below closes 01WS's forward direction. Nothing downstream has to argue about tensor
equivalences.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_dualBasisOne`: rank-one dual bases on a family
  of opens covering `X` make the closed subscheme an effective Cartier divisor.
* `Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_dualBasisOne`: the same criterion
  with the cover chosen pointwise, which is how a local computation presents itself.

## Implementation notes

Both statements are assembled from two existing results. Local data gives invertibility by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_of_dualBasisOne`: the evaluation pairing of the sheaf with
its dual is locally bijective, hence inverted by sheafification. That produces
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible`, which
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.toAlgebraicGeometry` converts into the
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible` that `Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor`
is defined by. On the Zariski site `Opens X` the sheafification hypotheses of the first result
are satisfied automatically, so the criterion needs no side conditions.

The covering condition is `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.CoversTop` for
`TopologicalSpace.Opens.grothendieckTopology`; `TopologicalSpace.Opens.coversTop_iff` turns it
into the statement that the opens cover the space, which is what the pointwise version uses.

These lemmas are about effective Cartier divisors in general, not about Chow homology; they are
stated here only because they were needed for Stacks Tag 02S4 (1), and belong in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Divisors/EffectiveCartier.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)

/-- The ideal sheaf of a closed subscheme, as a sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules. -/
abbrev idealSheafOfModules : SheafOfModules.{u}
    (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) :=
  Stacks.ClosedImmersion.idealSheaf I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom

/-- **A local criterion for an effective Cartier divisor.** If the ideal sheaf of a closed
subscheme admits a rank-one dual basis over each member of a family of opens covering `X`, then
the closed subscheme is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_dualBasisOne {Ix : Type u} (V : Ix → Opens X)
    (hV : (Opens.grothendieckTopology X).CoversTop V)
    (b : ∀ i, Stacks.SheafOfModules.DualBasisOne X.sheaf.obj
      (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property
      (idealSheafOfModules I) (V i)) :
    IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I :=
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_of_dualBasisOne _ _ hV b).toAlgebraicGeometry

/-- **A local criterion for an effective Cartier divisor, chosen pointwise.** If every point of
`X` has an open neighbourhood over which the ideal sheaf of a closed subscheme admits a
rank-one dual basis, then the closed subscheme is an effective Cartier divisor. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_dualBasisOne
    (h : ∀ x : X, ∃ V : Opens X, x ∈ V ∧
      Nonempty (Stacks.SheafOfModules.DualBasisOne X.sheaf.obj
        (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property
        (idealSheafOfModules I) V)) :
    IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I := by
  choose V hV b using h
  refine isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_dualBasisOne I V ?_ fun x => (b x).some
  refine (Opens.coversTop_iff X V).2 (IsOpenCover.mk ?_)
  ext y
  simpa using ⟨y, hV y⟩

end Stacks.Divisors

end
